---
source: crates/cli/tests/it/help.rs
expression: long_help(path)
---
Validate devlanes.yaml, or read and change the user config.yaml.

`check` validates the project's devlanes.yaml in this worktree. `get`, `set` and
`unset` act on the user config.yaml in the devlanes home (~/.devlanes, or
$DEVLANES_HOME), the settings this machine shares across projects; they work
without the daemon.

Usage: devlanes config [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  check  Validate this worktree's devlanes.yaml, including preset options
  get    Print a setting of the user config.yaml with defaults included; without a key, every setting
  set    Change a setting in the user config.yaml, keeping its comments; refuses invalid values
  unset  Remove a setting from the user config.yaml so its default applies again
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --json
          Print JSON: one document, or NDJSON for streams (same as --output json)

      --output <MODE>
          Output mode [default: agent when an AI agent runs devlanes, plain in CI or without a terminal, else human]

          Possible values:
          - human: Colors and symbols, for a terminal
          - plain: The same information without color, one line per event
          - agent: Terse lines for AI agents: failures first, with next commands, size-capped
          - json:  The daemon's data as JSON, or NDJSON for streams

      --project <PROJECT>
          Use this project instead of the one containing the current directory

      --lane <LANE>
          Use this lane ([project@]lane) instead of the current worktree's

      --yes
          Confirm actions that would ask first; needed when no terminal can prompt

      --quiet
          Print nothing on success; errors still go to stderr

      --env <KEY=VALUE>
          Set a variable for started processes (start, restart, run TASK, exec); repeatable

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Limit waits and streams, such as 30s, 5m or 1h [default for start and wait: 180s]

      --budget <BYTES>
          Cap agent-mode output at this many bytes [default: 16384, minimum: 256]

  -v, --verbose...
          Print timestamped diagnostics of the client and daemon to stderr; -vv for more [env: DEVLANES_VERBOSE=1|2]

Examples:
  devlanes config check                     validate this worktree's devlanes.yaml
  devlanes config get                       every user setting, defaults included
  devlanes config get proxy.https_port
  devlanes config set tui.theme dark
  devlanes config set tls.trust '[system, firefox]'
  devlanes config unset tui.theme           back to the default
